    "market_inefficiency": "A 20-bar Donchian break only becomes a tradeable dislocation when three conditions co-occur: (1) volume climax (vol_z20 elevated) proves resting liquidity is being consumed, (2) HTF slope has non-trivial magnitude so the cascade has directional drift, and (3) intraday ATR is expanded versus H1 ATR so continuation distance can exceed round-trip friction. Mild-volume flat-ATR breaks are the prior payoff attractor and are explicitly excluded.",
